From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HONOR ZQC-P M1010 user <adefka@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 May 2026 00:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: hda/realtek: Add quirk for HONOR ZQC-P M1010 headset mic

The HONOR MagicBook Pro 14 (2026), model M1010 with PCB ZQC-P, has the
Realtek ALC256 codec at PCI subsystem ID 1ee7:209d. The BIOS reports
pin 0x19 with the default 0x411111f0 ("Speaker at Ext Rear,
NO_PRESENCE"), which leaves the 3.5mm combo-jack headset microphone
unusable on Linux.

A simple ALC2XX_FIXUP_HEADSET_MIC entry like the sibling HONOR BRB-X
M1010 (1ee7:2078) uses turned out to be insufficient on this PCB: with
pincfg 0x03a1103c and only the PRE_PROBE branch of the fixup function,
pin 0x19's GET_PIN_SENSE returns 0 after every cold/warm boot and after
every S3/S4 resume, the SOF DSP capture path is never activated, and
`arecord -D plughw:0,0` records silence — only a manual unplug+replug
of the headset gets things going.

Use the canonical "no jack detect" pattern instead: pincfg 0x01a1913c
(JACK_DETECT_OVERRIDE=1, treat pin as always-present) chained to the
existing ALC269_FIXUP_HEADSET_MODE_NO_HP_MIC, whose
alc_fixup_headset_mode handler runs on PRE_PROBE + PROBE + INIT
(including after suspend/resume) and wires the analog mic path through
alc_probe_headset_mode / alc_update_headset_mode.

Verified live on hardware:
  * pin 0x19 GET_PIN_SENSE = 0x80000000 (presence=1) immediately after
    cold boot and after modprobe reload — no replug needed
  * `arecord -D plughw:0,0 -f S16_LE -r 48000 -c 2` captures clean speech
    (abs_max 32647, RMS 648, 0% clipping at +10dB Mic Boost)
  * PipeWire exposes HiFi__Mic2__source ("sof-hda-dsp Stereo Microphone")
    alongside the existing 4-channel DMIC source

Signed-off-by: HONOR ZQC-P M1010 user <adefka@gmail.com>
---
 sound/hda/codecs/realtek/alc269.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/hda/codecs/realtek/alc269.c b/sound/hda/codecs/realtek/alc269.c
index 0000000..0000001 100644
--- a/sound/hda/codecs/realtek/alc269.c
+++ b/sound/hda/codecs/realtek/alc269.c
@@ -4117,6 +4117,7 @@ enum {
 	ALC287_FIXUP_THINKPAD_I2S_SPK,
 	ALC287_FIXUP_MG_RTKC_CSAMP_CS35L41_I2C_THINKPAD,
 	ALC2XX_FIXUP_HEADSET_MIC,
+	ALC256_FIXUP_HONOR_ZQC_P_M1010_MIC,
 	ALC289_FIXUP_DELL_CS35L41_SPI_2,
 	ALC294_FIXUP_CS35L41_I2C_2,
 	ALC256_FIXUP_ACER_SFG16_MICMUTE_LED,
@@ -6512,6 +6513,16 @@ static const struct hda_fixup alc269_fixups[] = {
 		.type = HDA_FIXUP_FUNC,
 		.v.func = alc2xx_fixup_headset_mic,
 	},
+	[ALC256_FIXUP_HONOR_ZQC_P_M1010_MIC] = {
+		.type = HDA_FIXUP_PINS,
+		.v.pins = (const struct hda_pintbl[]) {
+			/* use as headset mic, without its own jack detect —
+			 * the ZQC-P PCB's impedance circuit on pin 0x19 is
+			 * unreliable across boot/resume cycles */
+			{ 0x19, 0x01a1913c },
+			{ }
+		},
+		.chained = true,
+		.chain_id = ALC269_FIXUP_HEADSET_MODE_NO_HP_MIC,
+	},
 	[ALC289_FIXUP_DELL_CS35L41_SPI_2] = {
 		.type = HDA_FIXUP_FUNC,
 		.v.func = cs35l41_fixup_spi_two,
@@ -7772,6 +7783,7 @@ static const struct snd_pci_quirk alc269_fixup_tbl[] = {
 	SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x1d72, 0x1947, "RedmiBook Air", ALC255_FIXUP_XIAOMI_HEADSET_MIC),
 	SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x1e39, 0xca14, "MEDION NM14LNL", ALC233_FIXUP_MEDION_MTL_SPK),
 	SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x1ee7, 0x2078, "HONOR BRB-X M1010", ALC2XX_FIXUP_HEADSET_MIC),
+	SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x1ee7, 0x209d, "HONOR ZQC-P M1010", ALC256_FIXUP_HONOR_ZQC_P_M1010_MIC),
 	SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x1f4c, 0xe001, "Minisforum V3 (SE)", ALC245_FIXUP_BASS_HP_DAC),
 	SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x1f66, 0x0105, "Ayaneo Portable Game Player", ALC287_FIXUP_CS35L41_I2C_2),
 	SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x2014, 0x800a, "Positivo ARN50", ALC269_FIXUP_LIMIT_INT_MIC_BOOST),
--
